      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would this in general be a suitable way to let the ScalerContext decide whether to apply emboldening or not? Some implementations for non-remote typefaces are missing and they should in general follow the DWrite implementation. It\u0027s a bit unfortunate that this would mean another flag.\n\nAlternatives considered: Join the previous glyphMaskNeedsForeGroundColor and this one into a new method that returns some high level font type in a bitfield (i.e. isColrV0, isColrV1, isColorBitmap, isColor...)\n\nIf you have other architectural ideas or suggestions, I\u0027d be quite happy. A fix is needed to address this Windows emboldening emoji presentation regression. \n\n\n",
      "revId": "6420bcc94a7670d4f37ae192901a2f692a966f5d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
